prompts.prompt:
Use case: identity-preserve. Asset: transparent sprite sheet for a 2-second 2D jump test. Reference image is the approved character and illustration style. Make ONE 3 columns by 2 rows sheet, landscape 1536x1024, six separate complete poses of this EXACT ginger and white Pomsky Ebi, all facing RIGHT, same camera, same physical scale and proportions, thin dark collar, pale blue eye, white forehead blaze, cream chest and socks, curled fluffy cream-tipped tail. Preserve approved face, body volume, linework, grouped fur shapes, flat warm cel shading and subtle paper texture. Each 512x512 cell contains one entire dog with generous transparent padding, no overlap.
Read left to right top then bottom:
1 standing alert, head looking up-right;
2 crouching before jump, hind legs loaded, front paws lowered, head up-right;
3 rising jump, body diagonally upright, front paws reaching forward, hind legs trailing, mouth slightly open;
4 apex of jump, upright reaching toward right with open mouth aimed right, bent forelegs;
5 descending jump, forepaws stretching down, mouth gently closed as if gripping a thin tray lip, NO tray drawn;
6 landed on floor, four paws, holding head proudly upward right, mouth gently closed as if gripping a thin tray lip, NO tray drawn.
No environment, no ground, no shadows, no eggs, no tray, no labels, no text, no borders, no extra dogs, no cropped paws. Genuinely transparent alpha outside the six dog silhouettes. This is an animation family not six redesigns. Keep body size consistent despite pose changes.
